  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_037, scvi_n200 + vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706) establishes that multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion, and vit_l are strong choices, and scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 by ~4%. However, scgpt—a fundamentally different generative RNA encoder—has never been tested in any multimodal configuration, leaving a major source of uncertainty about whether an alternative learned representation could match or exceed scvi_n200. This experiment (config_049: scgpt + vit_l + avgpool + weighted + multiprofile) isolates the RNA encoder as the single variable against the best-known settings for all other dimensions. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it reduces uncertainty on the highest-impact unexplored axis: if scgpt performs comparably, it opens a new search branch; if it underperforms significantly, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder and lets us concentrate remaining experiments on finer-grained choices (e.g., transformer vs avgpool with scvi_n200, or concat vs weighted)."
}

